# Fork Dos and Don'ts

Full reference: [docs/fork-guidelines.md](docs/fork-guidelines.md)

## Setup

- Node `>=22.18.0`, pnpm `11.3.0`, Docker, ≥12 GB RAM
- `./setup.sh` → `docker compose -f docker-compose-local.yml up` → `pnpm dev` (web:3000, admin:3001)
- Before ship: `pnpm check` (or `pnpm fix` + `pnpm check:types`); API tests via docker-compose-test.yml

## Code — DO

- Imports: `workspace:*` internal, `catalog:` external
- Strict TypeScript; oxfmt + OxLint (root `.oxlintrc.json` only)
- camelCase / PascalCase; MobX in `packages/shared-state`; UI in `@plane/ui`
- Unit tests for every feature/fix
- Design: Canvas → Surface → Layer; semantic text/border tokens; `bg-layer-X hover:bg-layer-X-hover`

## Code — DON'T

- No one-off ESLint configs; avoid `eslint-disable` unless necessary
- `bg-canvas` only at app root; no nested same-plane surfaces; match layer to surface
- No hardcoded colors when semantic tokens exist; no shipping without tests

## Git / PR — DO

- Branch: `<type>/<work-item-id>-<short-description>` (lowercase ID; don't invent IDs)
- Husky: oxfmt + OxLint `--deny-warnings` — fix and recommit; never skip hooks
- PR base: `preview`; title: `[WORK-ITEM-ID] <type>: <summary>`; fill PR template

## Git / PR — DON'T

- No `--no-verify`; no committing `.env`/secrets; no work-item ID at end of branch name

## i18n / security

- New keys in **all** locales; preserve ICU + full CLDR plurals
- Never translate brand/DNT terms (Plane, Power K, Intake, plan tiers, etc.)
- Security: report privately to security@plane.so only
